hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadafi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. H Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me that Ibn Wahb told them, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Ata bin Yazid Al-Laithi told him that Hamran, the client of Othman, informed him that one day Othman bin Affan called for ablution, so he performed it. So he washed his palms three times and rinsed his hair, then he washed his face three times, then he washed his right hand up to the elbow three times, then he washed his hand. His left foot is like that, then he wiped his head, then he washed his right foot up to the ankles three times, then he washed his left leg like that. That, then he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing an ablution similar to this ablution of mine. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then gets up and performs two rak’ahs without speaking to himself, his previous sins will be forgiven,” Ibn Shihab: Our scholars used to say: This ablution is the most effective ablution anyone can use for prayer."
